er put  uh a jumper on a tv why would you ever  put a jumper on a light  um but that stuff again didn't matter  because  i'm not really trying to tell a  narrative um i'm really trying to  express  a feeling so i you know things that when  working on the other short films that i  have planned to release which are  again way more narrative and character  focused i would never do again  um but for the purposes of this which  was a very experimental film  in a weird way again an expression of a  feeling  i don't feel like it's something that i  see that commonly i'm sure it's been  done to death i mean people told me when  they saw this that it was like the least  original concept of all time  uh that was probably the main criticism  i got but you know i've  not seen a single film that was based on  covert isolation  i have no doubt that plenty exist but  it's a  difficult thing to take as valuable  criticism when i had not seen any of  them  or even heard of them um even though in  my head i'm like of course people will  have made these like there's no way that  like students haven't been making these  for ages but i hadn't seen it so it's  like a thing that  an interesting criticism because i don't  know what i'm supposed to do with it  it's like well am i supposed to  not make something that i want to make  because other people have probably made  it  um though there were some fair  criticisms but you know regardless  moving on  stuff i would not do next time that i  was okay with in this instance  uh this one obviously the frame hang on  we go back to that  it gets more oppressive here um this is  intentionally brought down at that point  in time this is brought out  this is uh the contrast is obviously a  big shift here and i think  this might be the third shot that's  desaturated the desaturation starts here  right  so things start getting desaturated um  around this point and then this part is  intentionally  the only line of dialogue and also took  a long time 